// Go Fish — 3 players, ask any player for a rank you hold, lay down books
// (sets of four).
//
// Rules:
//   - 52-card deck; each player is dealt 7 cards.
//   - On your turn, ask **any player** for one rank **that you hold**: if
//     they hold any cards of that rank, they must hand them all over;
//     otherwise you draw one card from the deck (go fish). Ranks you do not
//     hold are not offered (standard rule).
//   - After the ask, you may lay down a book: four cards of the same rank.
//     The engine validates the chosen set against the `Book` combo (submit
//     0 cards to skip). Books land on your Books pile and score 4 points.
//   - The game ends when the deck runs out or a player empties their hand
//     (or after 24 turns); the most books wins.
//
// Engine notes (how the new capabilities are used):
//   - The ask is a 13-way `choose` (one option per rank — the DSL has no
//     "choose a value" expression yet); each option is guarded by
//     `"<Rank>" in Hand of current` so unheld ranks are no-ops. The chosen
//     rank is stored in the `AskRank` string memory (with an `AskFlag`
//     marker) instead of duplicating the ask logic 13 times; the transfer
//     and draw logic below runs once, reading `(&S:AskRank of current)`.
//   - The transfer uses `deal Hand where Rank is (&S:AskRank of current)
//     of any …` — a memory read in a where-filter plus the `SourcePlayerAny`
//     quantifier (2026-08-10) prompts a `ChoosePlayer` and substitutes the
//     choice, so you ask *any* player.
//   - Draw-on-miss uses a scratch-pile pattern: the transfer moves the
//     target's cards to the `Scratch` pile (empty set = no-op on a miss).
//     The draw check runs **before** the take: `if (Scratch empty)` draws
//     while the pile still reflects the ask result, then the take moves the
//     cards on a hit. (Inverting this order re-introduces draw-on-hit — the
//     take empties the pile, so a later `Scratch empty` check always fires.)
//   - Picking an unheld rank leaves `AskFlag` at 0, so the shared block is
//     skipped and the turn is wasted — the standard rule is preserved.
//   - Laying down uses the combo-source move (`ComboSource`): the player
//     picks cards from the whole hand and the engine validates them against
//     the combo filter, re-prompting on mismatch. `same Rank` matches any
//     duplicated rank, so a 2+2 split also passes the filter — a documented
//     simplification of the combo semantics (engine-vs-design.md D-16).
//   - Scoring is by books (4 points per book) instead of hand size.
//
// Remaining deviations (engine-gated, not authoring):
//   - The player prompt includes yourself — asking yourself wastes the turn
//     (the "any" candidates are all in-game players).
//   - A successful ask does not grant another ask — the engine has no
//     conditional re-ask loop inside a turn.
//   - The `Scratch` pile is a visible table location (a scratch pile is the
//     only way to reference a prompted player's cards in a condition).

player P1, P2, P3
turnorder (P:P1, P:P2, P:P3)
location Hand on all
location Books on all
location Deck on table
location Scratch on table
memory AskRank on all
memory AskFlag on all

combo Book where (same Rank and size >= 4)

card on Deck:
  Rank(Ace, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven, Eight, Nine, Ten, Jack, Queen, King)
    for Suit(Diamonds, Clubs, Hearts, Spades)

shuffle Deck

stage Deal for current 1 times {
  deal 7 from Deck private to Hand of all
}

stage Ask for current until (Deck empty or Hand of current empty) or 24 times {
  reset AskRank
  reset AskFlag
  choose {
    if ("Ace" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Ace"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Two" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Two"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Three" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Three"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Four" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Four"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Five" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Five"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Six" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Six"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Seven" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Seven"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Eight" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Eight"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Nine" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Nine"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Ten" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Ten"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Jack" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Jack"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("Queen" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "Queen"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
    or
    if ("King" in Hand of current) {
      AskRank is "King"
      AskFlag is 1
    }
  }
  if ((&I:AskFlag of current) == 1) {
    deal Hand where Rank is (&S:AskRank of current) of any private to Scratch
    if (Scratch empty) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
    if (not Scratch empty) {
      deal Scratch private to Hand of current
    }
  }
  if (not Book in Hand of current empty) {
    optional {
      move Book in Hand of current private to Books
    }
  }
  cycle to next
}

stage Score for current 3 times {
  score size(cards Books of current) to current
  cycle to next
}

stage End for current 1 times {
  winner is highest score
}
